# Alpha Release Report

Schema: `mpk.alpha_release_report.v0`

Status: post-Go/VIR-cutover

Milestone: `GO-VIR-02-T12`

## Result

The active Go source path uses the registered `go2vir` frontend, canonical VIR,
source-map and source-manifest validation, VC v1, policy v1, AI explanation v1,
and AI API v1. Removed predecessor interfaces have no runtime adapter, route,
flag, fixture, or production parser.

Certificate v0 and proof acceptance are unchanged. Go source, contracts,
release registries, compilers, frontend results, VIR, source maps, manifests,
VCs, policy reports, and AI output remain untrusted helper artifacts. Only
canonical certificates and checked theory certificates accepted by the
configured source-free checkers support proof acceptance.

## Active release evidence

`release-report.json` remains the canonical generated package/checker evidence
report. It records source-free and independent reference-checker results,
certificate/export/axiom hashes, axiom counts, and release-gate status. Verify
it without rewriting:

```sh
python3 scripts/generate-release-report.py --check
```

The Go/VIR corpus manifest is `fixtures/vir-go/manifest.json`. It records two
clean byte-identical generations, 100 alpha functions, positive and negative
frontend roots, example/VC coverage, checker agreement, and zero unresolved
semantic dispositions. The reviewed migration report is archived at
`develop/migrations/archive/go-gir-to-vir-report.md` and is never executed.

## Reproduction

```sh
./scripts/check-no-active-gir.sh --strict
./scripts/build-release-bundles.sh --check go
./scripts/check-release-bundles.sh --fixture go
./scripts/regenerate-go-vir-corpus.sh --check
cargo test -p mpk-cli --test frontend_runner
./scripts/check-fast.sh
./scripts/check-all.sh
(cd go-tools/go2vir && go test -count=1 ./...)
cargo test --workspace
python3 scripts/generate-release-report.py --check
git diff --check
```

